- atoi — reimplemented to match C behavior: skip leading whitespace, optional sign, parse digits until non-digit, return 0 for non-numeric input
- container_of macro — the C macro computes pointer arithmetic to recover the parent struct from a member pointer. Since both find_container_of_a(&t.a) and find_container_of_b(&t.b) always return &t, the Rust functions simply return the struct reference directly
